y home and Lina had saved me a plate of arroz con pollo from lunch. She'd had a slow afternoon — said the distributor raised prices on cooking oil again, which means she either eats the cost or marks up and risks losing her regulars. We talked about it for a bit. Not much to do about it.\n\nLogged my earnings in the notebook. Slightly above average for a Thursday. Bike needs new brake pads soon, I can hear them starting to grind. Priced them out at the shop near the house — forty-five mil, which is fine. I'll do it Saturday when I'm off."","- 2025-04-17 | Drift evidence | internal Schwartz label(s): Security | excerpt: "Week's been rough on the bike. The brake pads I was going to replace Saturday — didn't do it. Saturday got busy, Sunday Lina needed help at the tienda, Monday I forgot, and now it's Thursday and they're grinding metal on metal. I can feel the vibration through the handlebars when I stop.\n\nI know it's not smart. Every day I ride with bad brakes is a day something could go wrong, and fixing a bent rotor costs ten times what pads cost. I've been through this before, years ago, ended up paying three hundred mil because I waited too long. You'd think I'd learn.\n\nBut here's the thing — stopping for the repair means losing half a day of work, and this week the app has a streak bonus if I hit thirty deliveries by Friday. I'm at twenty-two. If I stop tomorrow to fix the bike I lose the streak and probably two hundred mil in bonus. So I keep telling myself one more day, one more day. Lina doesn't know the brakes are this bad. She'd tell me to fix them immediately, and she'd be right.""],"north_star_context":{"core_value_phrase":"Feeling calm and secure in my life","date":"2025-04-10","exact_quote":"Dropped the third app. Deleted it this morning, not worth the mental load. Back to the two I know.","mode":"reminder","source_id":"c876219a:entry:2","source_text":"Dropped the third app. Deleted it this morning, not worth the mental load. Back to the two I know.